{
  "bio_short": "NAOBA is the sound of Tamara Montenegro, a Nicaraguan producer, DJ and sound artist building a bridge between human technology and Earth technology: the deep, energetic intelligence we already carry inside us. Her music works like architecture made of frequency. Sub-bass pulses, ancestral rhythm and fine organic textures lock into geometric patterns, like sand drawing sacred shapes on a vibrating plate, so the sound is felt in the body as much as heard. On the dance floor it becomes ritual. In the studio it becomes a laboratory where psychoacoustics, code and intuition meet, and each set is a sequence of frequency codes that tunes the nervous system and returns people to their own inner signal. Her music was in consideration for the Latin Grammy 2026, her scores accompany films honoured at Diversity in Cannes, and her work has been presented at ISEA Dubai, Sound Art Festival Mexico City and TEDx.",
